1
00:00:47,422 --> 00:00:48,173
That's enough, Bok!

2
00:00:53,470 --> 00:00:54,554
Sianong!

3
00:00:55,764 --> 00:00:56,598
Sianong!

4
00:00:57,640 --> 00:00:59,642
It's not too late for Chiara.

5
00:01:01,102 --> 00:01:04,189
Chiara isn't the one
who's responsible for all of this.

6
00:01:04,272 --> 00:01:05,857
It's Vicky.

7
00:01:06,357 --> 00:01:08,401
You two go to Italy!

8
00:01:08,485 --> 00:01:09,486
I'm tired.

9
00:01:11,071 --> 00:01:11,905
Bok!

10
00:01:11,988 --> 00:01:12,947
Sianong!

11
00:01:13,031 --> 00:01:14,991
Sianong!

12
00:01:25,168 --> 00:01:28,421
I wish he had given us
a chance to help him.

13
00:01:28,505 --> 00:01:31,424
But that doesn't justify betraying us.

14
00:01:31,508 --> 00:01:33,009
He was also a victim of a system

15
00:01:33,092 --> 00:01:34,886
that made him believe
he had no other choice.

16
00:01:34,969 --> 00:01:36,888
We need to bring down the system

17
00:01:36,971 --> 00:01:38,473
that creates people like him.

18
00:01:39,891 --> 00:01:40,892
<i>And the Concordat.</i>

19
00:01:44,729 --> 00:01:46,523
- Definitely Italy.
- Italy?

20
00:01:47,941 --> 00:01:49,734
So, what are you going to do in Italy?

21
00:01:49,818 --> 00:01:51,653
I have some friends there too.

22
00:01:53,404 --> 00:01:54,906
The Castellanis.

23
00:01:54,989 --> 00:01:57,242
One day, I'll take you there.

24
00:01:57,325 --> 00:01:58,368
Now I know why in Italy.

25
00:01:58,451 --> 00:02:00,453
- Why?
- Sianong has friends there.

26
00:02:01,830 --> 00:02:02,747
Castellani?

27
00:02:02,831 --> 00:02:05,333
If that's Sianong's last clue to us,

28
00:02:05,416 --> 00:02:08,086
those are the people he wants us to find.

29
00:02:09,754 --> 00:02:10,839
Mom.

30
00:02:11,840 --> 00:02:13,508
Want to go shopping?

31
00:02:17,095 --> 00:02:18,555
My in-law texted.

32
00:02:19,931 --> 00:02:20,974
Tess.

33
00:02:21,057 --> 00:02:22,225
It's like

34
00:02:23,184 --> 00:02:24,727
she's sensing something

35
00:02:25,603 --> 00:02:26,688
about what happened.

36
00:02:27,397 --> 00:02:29,315
About what happened between you and Mikoy.

37
00:02:30,900 --> 00:02:32,068
What did she say?

38
00:02:47,959 --> 00:02:48,877
You know that?

39
00:02:53,172 --> 00:02:54,007
You're right.

40
00:02:56,843 --> 00:02:58,344
So what did you reply?

41
00:02:58,428 --> 00:02:59,387
What?

42
00:03:00,013 --> 00:03:01,055
I just hearted it, Chiara,

43
00:03:01,139 --> 00:03:03,600
because I didn't know what to say.

44
00:03:03,683 --> 00:03:05,935
I might say the wrong thing. Better not.

45
00:03:37,592 --> 00:03:38,468
Mama Yaya.

46
00:03:39,052 --> 00:03:39,969
Rahmboy.

47
00:03:40,845 --> 00:03:41,679
Chiara.

48
00:03:48,228 --> 00:03:49,229
Sianong…

49
00:03:49,312 --> 00:03:50,355
He's gone.

50
00:03:52,857 --> 00:03:54,567
He was careless.

51
00:03:54,651 --> 00:03:56,903
That's how the agency caught him.

52
00:03:57,487 --> 00:03:58,446
They chased him,

53
00:03:59,948 --> 00:04:01,991
and while he was trying to escape,

54
00:04:02,575 --> 00:04:03,493
he got into an accident.

55
00:04:07,997 --> 00:04:10,333
Human life is so fragile

56
00:04:10,416 --> 00:04:12,168
in this world of ours.

57
00:04:12,252 --> 00:04:13,544
Haven't you gotten used to it?

58
00:04:17,840 --> 00:04:19,008
I'm used to it.

59
00:04:21,803 --> 00:04:24,013
Well, is this going to be a problem?

60
00:04:24,681 --> 00:04:25,723
No.

61
00:04:26,683 --> 00:04:29,018
He can't talk now, so there won't be.

62
00:04:30,061 --> 00:04:32,563
Honestly, I thought about it too.

63
00:04:33,231 --> 00:04:35,316
It's better that Sianong is gone

64
00:04:35,400 --> 00:04:39,737
because I know he was the one
who hated Mikoy the most.

65
00:04:39,821 --> 00:04:41,322
Now that he's gone,

66
00:04:41,406 --> 00:04:43,074
Mikoy is safer.

67
00:04:44,117 --> 00:04:45,493
Isn't that what you wanted?

68
00:04:49,080 --> 00:04:50,164
How is he?

69
00:04:51,624 --> 00:04:52,709
Mikoy?

70
00:04:53,751 --> 00:04:54,585
He's still alive.

71
00:05:07,181 --> 00:05:09,892
he has no way of getting to you anymore.

72
00:05:11,644 --> 00:05:13,563
That's probably for the best.

73
00:05:13,646 --> 00:05:15,398
With everything that's happening,

74
00:05:16,607 --> 00:05:19,652
he may be moving on too.

75
00:05:57,982 --> 00:06:01,235
the Castellani family
was first known for their jewelry.

76
00:06:05,698 --> 00:06:07,450
their family business was at risk.

77
00:06:08,242 --> 00:06:10,787
And eventually, they slowly integrated
themselves into the mafia world,

78
00:06:10,870 --> 00:06:11,746
just to survive.

79
00:06:12,455 --> 00:06:14,082
And it seems like it all paid off

80
00:06:14,165 --> 00:06:18,169
because currently,
the new generation of Castellanis

81
00:06:18,252 --> 00:06:21,130
is the biggest threat
to the Concordat's leadership.

82
00:06:21,631 --> 00:06:24,717
Well, aside from looking like models,

83
00:06:24,801 --> 00:06:27,845
the Castellanis certainly
have a strong presence.

84
00:06:30,264 --> 00:06:32,016
Appeal isn't all they have.

85
00:06:43,611 --> 00:06:46,280
the Castellanis are currently
negotiating with Chiara.

86
00:06:51,911 --> 00:06:54,413
Mom, Chiara, I'll go ahead.

87
00:06:54,497 --> 00:06:55,373
Okay, dear.

88
00:06:58,251 --> 00:06:59,335
Jeez.

89
00:06:59,418 --> 00:07:02,130
They rejected our counteroffer again.

90
00:07:02,964 --> 00:07:04,173
Yes, Chiara.

91
00:07:04,257 --> 00:07:05,633
They still won't agree.

92
00:07:05,716 --> 00:07:07,093
They're so conniving.

93
00:07:10,388 --> 00:07:12,473
Why don't they want to come
to an agreement?

94
00:07:12,557 --> 00:07:14,684
What do they really want?

95
00:07:15,518 --> 00:07:18,479
Your position, of course, dear.

96
00:07:19,480 --> 00:07:22,567
Before you took over,
what the Castellanis wanted

97
00:07:22,650 --> 00:07:26,863
was to lead and control the Concordat.

98
00:07:26,946 --> 00:07:28,656
But that didn't happen.

99
00:07:29,365 --> 00:07:31,117
So they're extremely bitter about it.

100
00:07:33,411 --> 00:07:34,745
So they're causing trouble

101
00:07:34,829 --> 00:07:38,291
just because they can't accept
that I'm now the leader of the Concordat?

102
00:07:44,130 --> 00:07:47,258
Guys are indeed hard to understand.

103
00:07:47,341 --> 00:07:48,676
So stressful.

104
00:07:56,058 --> 00:07:59,645
So they're not fans
of Chiara's leadership?

105
00:08:00,229 --> 00:08:04,358
I think it's not just because
the Castellanis have appeal or influence.

106
00:08:13,576 --> 00:08:14,702
You're right, Dara.

107
00:08:15,244 --> 00:08:17,580
In fact, that's the trend these days.

108
00:09:21,769 --> 00:09:22,728
Can I use the phone?

109
00:09:23,271 --> 00:09:24,105
Sure, sir.

110
00:09:24,188 --> 00:09:25,815
No one's really using it anymore.

111
00:09:25,898 --> 00:09:27,608
Everyone just chats now.

112
00:09:27,692 --> 00:09:28,818
Thanks.

113
00:09:45,501 --> 00:09:46,419
I know they are in Italy.

114
00:09:46,502 --> 00:09:49,046
But Italy is too big,
and I don't have enough time.

115
00:09:49,130 --> 00:09:51,299
If I have to know something
as soon as possible,

116
00:09:51,382 --> 00:09:52,300
then tell me now.

117
00:10:13,029 --> 00:10:13,946
What's this?

118
00:10:14,614 --> 00:10:16,073
You're making a move on your own?

119
00:10:17,450 --> 00:10:18,909
And who were you talking to?

120
00:10:19,785 --> 00:10:21,120
My asset.

121
00:10:22,913 --> 00:10:23,748
Wow.

122
00:10:23,831 --> 00:10:25,291
And since when did you have an asset?

123
00:10:25,875 --> 00:10:27,627
That's not important anymore, Alex.

124
00:10:27,710 --> 00:10:28,794
What do you mean, it's not?

125
00:10:29,462 --> 00:10:30,796
Are you sure about this?

126
00:10:31,339 --> 00:10:32,298
And who is this person?

127
00:10:32,882 --> 00:10:34,258
They might get you into trouble.

128
00:10:34,342 --> 00:10:36,844
Just leave me alone, Alex.
I know what I'm doing.

129
00:10:40,056 --> 00:10:41,182
Just let me have this one.

130
00:10:41,849 --> 00:10:43,684
It's safer if you don't know who they are.

131
00:10:43,768 --> 00:10:45,770
What matters is I can reach him
through the landline,

132
00:10:45,853 --> 00:10:47,563
and he gives me vital information.

133
00:11:01,911 --> 00:11:02,745
‪Oh.

134
00:11:03,454 --> 00:11:04,288
What's the problem?

135
00:11:04,372 --> 00:11:05,873
- What happened?
- What happened?

136
00:11:05,956 --> 00:11:07,792
What happened? Why?

137
00:11:14,590 --> 00:11:16,050
What did they say?

138
00:11:20,930 --> 00:11:22,890
they want to meet me.

139
00:11:27,728 --> 00:11:30,147
Finally, they're willing to talk.

140
00:11:31,065 --> 00:11:31,982
What's so good about it?

141
00:11:32,066 --> 00:11:33,526
What if they have a different agenda?

142
00:11:33,609 --> 00:11:34,985
What if-- What if they suddenly…

143
00:11:35,069 --> 00:11:36,612
Ambush! What if they ambush us?

144
00:11:36,695 --> 00:11:38,447
It's dangerous, dear. Don't do it!

145
00:11:38,531 --> 00:11:39,740
You're being dramatic.

146
00:11:39,824 --> 00:11:42,993
You're being way too negative.
It's just a meeting, dear.

147
00:11:43,077 --> 00:11:45,830
Dear, you know I never lie to you.

148
00:11:45,913 --> 00:11:48,249
You know those Castellanis,
they are cunning.

149
00:11:49,500 --> 00:11:51,419
We're going to prepare.

150
00:11:52,336 --> 00:11:54,547
They're cunning? That's their reputation.

151
00:11:54,630 --> 00:11:55,923
We won't back out.

152
00:12:32,418 --> 00:12:34,170
Italy is huge.

153
00:12:34,253 --> 00:12:35,421
Where in Italy?

154
00:12:37,923 --> 00:12:39,925
But are you sure Chiara Valtrovi will go?

155
00:12:42,595 --> 00:12:43,512
Yes, Mikoy.

156
00:12:43,596 --> 00:12:45,848
Isn't it dangerous for Chiara

157
00:12:45,931 --> 00:12:48,142
to meet with the Castellanis?

158
00:12:59,320 --> 00:13:00,154
Rahmboy, dear.

159
00:13:00,237 --> 00:13:02,490
You go with Chiara,

160
00:13:02,573 --> 00:13:06,911
so the Castellanis can see
that we're training

161
00:13:06,994 --> 00:13:10,748
new generation of mafia leaders
just like them.

162
00:13:37,775 --> 00:13:40,903
That's why the Moravianos
don't take you seriously,

163
00:13:41,862 --> 00:13:43,697
if you're going to be
this cowardly, Viktor!

164
00:13:58,796 --> 00:14:01,632
I'm the one who thinks things through.

165
00:14:01,715 --> 00:14:04,885
Between the two of us,
I'm the one who takes action.

166
00:14:08,764 --> 00:14:10,182
You're so funny, you know that?

167
00:14:10,683 --> 00:14:14,186
You have no right
to take action or make decisions.

168
00:14:19,441 --> 00:14:21,986
You're just sticking your nose
in all this.

169
00:14:23,028 --> 00:14:24,655
Oh, I'm just sticking my nose in?

170
00:14:25,698 --> 00:14:28,909
You rich and powerful people,

171
00:14:29,493 --> 00:14:33,038
you think you have this huge illusion

172
00:14:33,122 --> 00:14:35,583
that you're the ones
who make everything happen.

173
00:14:35,666 --> 00:14:38,502
But if it weren't for us poor people

174
00:14:38,586 --> 00:14:40,546
doing the work for you,

175
00:14:40,629 --> 00:14:41,797
you'd have nothing!

176
00:14:45,593 --> 00:14:49,179
We're just wasting time
because you two keep arguing.

177
00:14:54,560 --> 00:14:56,103
Rahmboy, you're coming with me.

178
00:15:20,836 --> 00:15:24,423
Are you telling me, Mikoy,
that you're getting all of this

179
00:15:24,506 --> 00:15:26,342
from your secret asset?

180
00:15:29,053 --> 00:15:30,179
There you go again.

181
00:15:32,973 --> 00:15:36,518
How can you say that your intel is legit?

182
00:15:36,602 --> 00:15:39,730
We don't even know who your asset is.

183
00:15:41,982 --> 00:15:43,192
You have a point, sir.

184
00:15:43,275 --> 00:15:46,654
We just got a little excited
about the information he has.

185
00:15:48,572 --> 00:15:50,658
I'm skeptical too, just like you.

186
00:15:55,996 --> 00:15:57,206
See? You get it now?

187
00:16:00,709 --> 00:16:04,338
Even though Chiara
is now the leader of the Concordat,

188
00:16:04,421 --> 00:16:09,343
she wouldn't risk her life
or the lives of her people

189
00:16:09,426 --> 00:16:11,720
to meet with a group

190
00:16:11,804 --> 00:16:15,182
that clearly doesn't
want her leading them.

191
00:16:16,809 --> 00:16:18,394
With all due respect, sir,

192
00:16:19,144 --> 00:16:20,896
you don't know Chiara.

193
00:16:21,772 --> 00:16:22,940
You don't understand her.

194
00:16:32,700 --> 00:16:33,784
Dear.

195
00:16:37,287 --> 00:16:39,081
Do not go, please.

196
00:16:39,665 --> 00:16:40,541
Remember,

197
00:16:46,296 --> 00:16:47,172
He's right, dear.

198
00:16:48,173 --> 00:16:49,425
Listen to your father.

199
00:16:54,930 --> 00:16:56,557
Whatever happened between Chiara and me,

200
00:16:57,141 --> 00:16:58,600
we still have a history.

201
00:16:59,184 --> 00:17:00,978
And that's my advantage over all of you.

202
00:17:02,271 --> 00:17:04,356
I'm sorry my asset is top secret.

203
00:17:05,065 --> 00:17:07,234
Maybe in time, you'll understand why.

204
00:17:10,237 --> 00:17:11,071
She's different.

205
00:17:12,239 --> 00:17:15,117
She wants every move she makes
to make a statement.

206
00:17:19,163 --> 00:17:21,540
Especially now that
she's the leader of the Concordat.

207
00:17:21,623 --> 00:17:24,043
She needs to prove through her actions

208
00:17:39,183 --> 00:17:40,642
But things are different now.

209
00:17:47,107 --> 00:17:49,568
What would they think of me?

210
00:17:53,072 --> 00:17:55,699
but the other Concordat groups as well.

211
00:17:55,783 --> 00:17:57,826
I'm sure all of them are waiting

212
00:18:15,344 --> 00:18:16,595
you're saying that

213
00:18:16,678 --> 00:18:19,431
Chiara is really going to Italy?

214
00:18:19,515 --> 00:18:21,266
I have a strong feeling she is, sir.

215
00:18:29,650 --> 00:18:30,818
Well, if that's the case,

216
00:18:31,819 --> 00:18:33,946
then all we have to do
is wait for Chiara Valtrovi

217
00:18:34,029 --> 00:18:35,364
when she goes to Italy.

218
00:18:35,447 --> 00:18:36,573
Exactly!

219
00:18:37,407 --> 00:18:39,326
This is our golden window.

220
00:18:45,791 --> 00:18:49,211
How can we make sure
Chiara will cooperate with us?

221
00:18:50,796 --> 00:18:51,630
Exactly, Mikoy.

222
00:18:51,713 --> 00:18:53,132
What if Chiara refuses to cooperate?

223
00:18:53,757 --> 00:18:55,217
Or refuses to be caught.

224
00:18:55,884 --> 00:18:56,718
What?

225
00:18:56,802 --> 00:18:58,470
You'll be playing cat and mouse in Italy.

226
00:18:58,554 --> 00:19:01,056
Or worse, it'll be catch me if you can
all over Europe.

227
00:19:02,808 --> 00:19:03,892
Impossible.

228
00:19:03,976 --> 00:19:05,769
We don't have the budget for that.

229
00:19:08,438 --> 00:19:09,606
Back in Hong Kong,

230
00:19:10,190 --> 00:19:11,483
even though you tried to escape from us,

231
00:19:11,567 --> 00:19:14,027
you still cooperated with us
even while the two of you were together.

232
00:19:14,736 --> 00:19:16,363
You had an agreement, and eventually,

233
00:19:18,282 --> 00:19:20,576
you ended up
with very important information

234
00:19:20,659 --> 00:19:22,119
in exchange for a day.

235
00:19:26,790 --> 00:19:28,083
she won't back down.

236
00:19:34,965 --> 00:19:38,343
She managed to escape
our law enforcement agency here.

237
00:19:39,636 --> 00:19:41,346
And it seems impossible

238
00:19:41,430 --> 00:19:44,349
that we can persuade her
to come back to our country.

239
00:19:46,977 --> 00:19:49,438
Who came up with the idea
of going to Italy

240
00:19:49,521 --> 00:19:51,607
to shake hands with criminals?

241
00:19:51,690 --> 00:19:52,691
Mikoy.

242
00:19:52,774 --> 00:19:56,028
Didn't we agree
that we're there to get Chiara Valtrovi?

243
00:20:36,318 --> 00:20:37,194
Ouch!

244
00:20:41,406 --> 00:20:42,407
Are you okay?

245
00:20:44,243 --> 00:20:45,994
Me? Of course, I'm more than okay.

246
00:20:46,745 --> 00:20:49,289
I may endure some body pains,

247
00:20:49,915 --> 00:20:52,417
but at least I've got
plenty of tricks up my sleeve.

248
00:20:52,501 --> 00:20:54,127
Right? Thanks to you.

249
00:21:01,176 --> 00:21:02,844
That's the spirit.

250
00:21:02,928 --> 00:21:05,180
That's the fighting spirit I want to see.

251
00:21:07,975 --> 00:21:09,977
But tell me something, Rahmboy.

252
00:21:12,729 --> 00:21:14,648
Can I trust you?

253
00:21:15,607 --> 00:21:16,566
Trust?

254
00:21:17,067 --> 00:21:17,985
Me?

255
00:21:18,068 --> 00:21:19,278
Of course!

256
00:21:21,488 --> 00:21:23,240
You really doubt me now?

257
00:21:25,325 --> 00:21:27,202
I heard that

258
00:21:27,286 --> 00:21:28,745
you've been having second thoughts.

259
00:21:29,288 --> 00:21:30,580
That you're not fully committed.

260
00:21:31,081 --> 00:21:31,915
Is that true?

261
00:21:33,417 --> 00:21:34,584
Chiara.

262
00:21:35,544 --> 00:21:37,004
I'm fully committed.

263
00:21:38,255 --> 00:21:41,049
There are probably still things
I need to learn, but…

264
00:21:42,301 --> 00:21:43,135
I'm ready.

265
00:21:43,927 --> 00:21:44,928
And remember this.

266
00:21:48,015 --> 00:21:49,308
We're on the same side.

267
00:21:50,767 --> 00:21:52,311
You can count on me, Chiara.

268
00:22:01,028 --> 00:22:02,738
But I want you to remember this too.

269
00:22:04,281 --> 00:22:05,532
I'm on your side.

270
00:22:07,409 --> 00:22:10,620
If you have any doubts,
it's better to tell me.

271
00:22:11,121 --> 00:22:13,248
Because from now on,

272
00:22:14,541 --> 00:22:16,460
you're my responsibility.

273
00:22:21,673 --> 00:22:22,507
Okay.

274
00:23:04,466 --> 00:23:08,178
But my gut feel tells me
that this isn't an ordinary mission.

275
00:23:08,261 --> 00:23:09,971
We're going to a place

276
00:23:10,055 --> 00:23:14,142
where the most powerful mafia
are gathering for a meeting.

277
00:23:14,226 --> 00:23:16,103
One mistake there,

278
00:23:16,186 --> 00:23:17,187
and we're all dead.

279
00:23:20,440 --> 00:23:23,401
In the mafia life,
there's always one problem after another.

280
00:23:23,485 --> 00:23:24,611
Look at me.

281
00:23:24,694 --> 00:23:28,073
La Morte Bianca raised me and trained me.

282
00:23:28,156 --> 00:23:28,990
But…

283
00:23:29,074 --> 00:23:31,034
I still managed to stand against her.

284
00:23:31,118 --> 00:23:35,372
For now, let's focus on the Castellanis.

285
00:23:35,455 --> 00:23:39,167
We know how cunning they are.
So let's be careful.

286
00:23:42,170 --> 00:23:43,839
You've been staring
into space for a while now.

287
00:23:43,922 --> 00:23:45,924
I was just thinking about your brother.

288
00:23:46,007 --> 00:23:49,136
But you know,
no matter how heavy the burden is,

289
00:23:49,219 --> 00:23:51,721
I'm sure he'll get through all of it.

290
00:23:51,805 --> 00:23:55,642
Why don't we show him that we're here,
that we support him?

291
00:23:56,434 --> 00:23:57,352
I have an idea.

292
00:23:57,435 --> 00:23:58,895
Hello, Captain Pepe.

293
00:23:58,979 --> 00:24:01,314
I was hoping to ask you a favor.
